From 14ec41007eafc0a1efcb2875d056ada7d65fb36e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:22:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ci): [daveey] drop stale windows-footgun marker in
 kanban_selfwork_outbound

Main a21b92cffd4d is red: tests/scripts/test_footgun_multiline_subprocess_encoding.py::
test_no_stale_multiline_suppression_markers flags hermes_cli/kanban_selfwork_outbound.py:80.

Why: 6b5122b22e94 added 'text=True,  # windows-footgun: ok (encoding on next line)'
while #3340 (19fc51c46476) taught the rule to read the call's continuation lines and
added a guard forbidding such now-redundant markers. The two landed 5 min apart.

Fix: remove the marker; encoding='utf-8' is on the next line of the same call, so the
rule no longer flags it.

Proof: RED on main CI run 43738491871 job 132886551534 (only failure: this test,
offender ...outbound.py:80). GREEN locally: test file 10 passed, 0 failed.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_selfwork_outbound.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/hermes_cli/kanban_selfwork_outbound.py b/hermes_cli/kanban_selfwork_outbound.py
index e13d3e3f442b864222a2bc2396133fbdb2622fd2..244b22a285e24a74e1d5c86830be2320a1fd41dd 100644
--- a/hermes_cli/kanban_selfwork_outbound.py
+++ b/hermes_cli/kanban_selfwork_outbound.py
@@ -77,7 +77,7 @@ def submit(args):
         route = [home['gateway'], 'tasks', home['profile'] + '/' + home['board'], 'selfwork-create']
     argv = ['hermes-hub', 'request', *route, '--id', request_id, '--args-file', '-']
     try:
-        result = subprocess.run(argv, input=json.dumps(body), capture_output=True, text=True,  # windows-footgun: ok (encoding on next line)
+        result = subprocess.run(argv, input=json.dumps(body), capture_output=True, text=True,
                                 encoding='utf-8', timeout=30, check=False, env=build_subprocess_env())
     except (OSError, subprocess.TimeoutExpired) as exc:
         raise SelfWorkError('self-work transport unavailable; retry the same request, never create locally') from exc
